\verb{(beta, b)} alone is INCOMPLETE. \code{A} carries the loading columns
too, through \code{rr_jacobians()}, and \code{coef_pos} names their \code{theta}
rows; a caller therefore gets the whole delta method rather than
discovering a missing piece.
